IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), Chapter 3 Part 1: drafting standards and consultation (sections 16, 17 and 19).
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
-- Same conventions as lga-register.l4: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no), NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- Whether consultation is "appropriate" or "reasonably practicable" is a judgment the text gives to the rule-maker: it is a plain input.

§ `Section 16: measures to achieve high drafting standards`

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:690 | (1) To encourage high standards in the drafting of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments, the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to promote the legal effectiveness, clarity, and intelligibility to anticipated users, of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments.
@ref s 16(1) (src:690-690)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(1): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to promote the legal effectiveness, clarity and intelligibility of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments` MEANS TRUE

DECLARE `Step for section 16(2)` IS ONE OF
    `undertaking or supervising the drafting of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments`
    `scrutinising preliminary drafts`
    `providing advice concerning the drafting`
    `providing training in drafting and related matters to officers and employees of Departments or other agencies`
    `arranging the temporary secondment of APS employees in the Office of Parliamentary Counsel to Departments or other agencies`
    `providing drafting precedents to officers and employees of Departments or other agencies`
    `any other step`

-- "may include, but are not limited to": a step not listed is NOTHING.
-- src:691 | (2) The steps referred to in subsection (1) may include, but are not limited to:
-- src:692 | (a) undertaking or supervising the drafting of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments; and
-- src:693 | (b) scrutinising preliminary drafts of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments; and
-- src:694 | (c) providing advice concerning the drafting of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments; and
-- src:695 | (d) providing training in drafting and matters related to drafting to officers and employees of Departments or other agencies; and
-- src:696 | (e) arranging the temporary secondment to Departments or other agencies of APS employees performing duties in the Office of Parliamentary Counsel; and
-- src:697 | (f) providing drafting precedents to officers and employees of Departments or other agencies.
@ref s 16(2) (src:691-697)
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Step for section 16(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(2): the steps referred to in subsection (1) may include the step` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `any other step` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `undertaking or supervising the drafting of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `scrutinising preliminary drafts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `providing advice concerning the drafting` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `providing training in drafting and related matters to officers and employees of Departments or other agencies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `arranging the temporary secondment of APS employees in the Office of Parliamentary Counsel to Departments or other agencies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `providing drafting precedents to officers and employees of Departments or other agencies` THEN JUST TRUE

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:698 | (3) The First Parliamentary Counsel must also cause steps to be taken:
-- src:699 | (a) to prevent the use of gender-specific language in legislative instruments and notifiable instruments in circumstances where it is not necessary to identify persons by their sex; and
-- src:700 | (b) to advise rule-makers for registered legislative instruments or notifiable instruments if those instruments use gender-specific language in those circumstances; and
-- src:701 | (c) to notify both Houses of the Parliament about any occasion when a rule-maker is advised under paragraph (b).
@ref s 16(3) (src:698-701)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(3)(a): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to prevent gender-specific language where it is not necessary to identify persons by their sex` MEANS TRUE

@ref s 16(3)(b) (src:700-700)
GIVEN `the instrument is a registered legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it uses gender-specific language in circumstances where it is not necessary to identify persons by their sex` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(3)(b): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to advise the rule-maker` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is a registered legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` AND `it uses gender-specific language in circumstances where it is not necessary to identify persons by their sex` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 16(3)(c) (src:701-701)
GIVEN `a rule-maker is advised under paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(3)(c): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to notify both Houses of the Parliament` MEANS
    IF `a rule-maker is advised under paragraph (b)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 17 and 19: consultation before a legislative instrument is made`

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the rule-maker
-- src:703 | (1) Before a legislative instrument is made, the rule-maker must be satisfied that there has been undertaken any consultation that is:
-- src:704 | (a) considered by the rule-maker to be appropriate; and
-- src:705 | (b) reasonably practicable to undertake.
@ref s 17(1) (src:703-705)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument has not yet been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(1): the rule-maker must be satisfied that the consultation the rule-maker considers appropriate, and that is reasonably practicable, has been undertaken` MEANS
    IF `it is a legislative instrument` AND `the instrument has not yet been made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (2): "may have regard to any relevant matter, including ...": a matter that is relevant is JUST TRUE; the two listed are relevant.
-- src:706 | (2) In determining whether any consultation that was undertaken is appropriate, the rule-maker may have regard to any relevant matter, including the extent to which the consultation:
-- src:707 | (a) drew on the knowledge of persons having expertise in fields relevant to the proposed instrument; and
-- src:708 | (b) ensured that persons likely to be affected by the proposed instrument had an adequate opportunity to comment on its proposed content.
@ref s 17(2) (src:706-708)
GIVEN `it is a matter relevant to whether the consultation was appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(2): the rule-maker may have regard to the matter` MEANS
    IF `it is a matter relevant to whether the consultation was appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:709 | (3) Without limiting, by implication, the form that consultation referred to in subsection (1) might take, such consultation could involve notification, either directly or by advertisement, of bodies that, or of organisations representative of persons who, are likely to be affected by the proposed instrument. Such notification could invite submissions to be made by a specified date or might invite participation in public hearings to be held concerning the proposed instrument.
@ref s 17(3) (src:709-709)
GIVEN `the consultation involves notification, directly or by advertisement, of bodies or organisations likely to be affected by the proposed instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(3): the consultation could involve the notification` MEANS
    IF `the consultation involves notification, directly or by advertisement, of bodies or organisations likely to be affected by the proposed instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:712 | The fact that consultation does not occur does not affect the validity or enforceability of a legislative instrument.
@ref s 19 (src:712-712)
GIVEN `consultation does not occur` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19: the failure to consult affects the validity or enforceability of the legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF `consultation does not occur` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
